---
import LegalPage from "../components/LegalPage.astro";
import { SITE, isSet } from "../config/site";
import { route } from "../config/routes";
const contact = route("contact");
---
<LegalPage title="Privacy Policy | Local Search Pro" heading="Privacy Policy" description="How Local Search Pro collects, uses and protects your personal information.">
  <p>This policy explains how Local Search Pro ("we", "us", "our") collects and uses personal information when you visit <strong>www.localsearchpro.co.uk</strong>, contact us or sign up for our services. We are the "data controller" for that information under UK data protection law.</p>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    Local Search Pro provides pay monthly websites, Google Business Profile management and local SEO services to small businesses in the UK.
    {isSet(SITE.legalName) && <> We trade as {SITE.legalName}.</>}
    {isSet(SITE.address) && <> Our address is {SITE.address}.</>}
  </p>
  <p>To contact us about this policy or your personal information, use our <a href={contact}>contact form</a>{isSet(SITE.email) && <> or email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a></>}.</p>

  <h2>What information we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Information you give us.</strong> When you use our contact or signup forms we collect your name, email address, and any of the following that you choose to provide: phone number, business name, current website address, the package you are interested in, and your message.</li>
    <li><strong>Information about your business.</strong> If you become a customer, we will also collect the details we need to provide the service, such as your business information, website content, logo and images, and access to relevant accounts (for example your Google Business Profile or website).</li>
    <li><strong>Technical information.</strong> Like most websites, our hosting provider automatically records technical information when you visit, such as your IP address, browser type, device and the pages requested. This is used to deliver the site and keep it secure.</li>
    <li><strong>Correspondence.</strong> Records of emails and other messages between you and us.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not knowingly collect personal information from children, and our services are aimed at businesses.</p>

  <h2>How and why we use your information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To reply to your enquiry and give you the information you asked for. <em>Legal basis: our legitimate interests in running our business and responding to enquiries, or taking steps at your request before entering into a contract.</em></li>
    <li>To set up and provide the services you sign up for, and to manage payments and your account. <em>Legal basis: performing our contract with you.</em></li>
    <li>To keep our website secure and working properly. <em>Legal basis: our legitimate interests.</em></li>
    <li>To meet legal, accounting and tax obligations. <em>Legal basis: legal obligation.</em></li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell your personal information. We will not use your details for marketing unless you have agreed to it or the law otherwise allows.</p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>We only share personal information where we need to, with:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Service providers</strong> that help us run the website and our business, such as website hosting and form processing (our website and forms are provided through Netlify), email, and payment providers. They may only use your information to provide their services to us.</li>
    <li><strong>Professional advisers</strong>, such as accountants and legal advisers, where needed.</li>
    <li><strong>Authorities</strong>, where we are required to by law.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Some of our providers are based outside the UK. Where your information is transferred outside the UK, we make sure appropriate safeguards are in place, such as an adequacy decision or approved standard contractual clauses.</p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>We keep personal information only for as long as we need it for the purposes above. Enquiries are kept for as long as needed to deal with them and for a reasonable period afterwards. Customer and payment records are kept for as long as our contract with you lasts and afterwards for as long as the law requires, for example for tax and accounting purposes.</p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under UK data protection law you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>ask for a copy of the personal information we hold about you;</li>
    <li>ask us to correct information that is inaccurate or incomplete;</li>
    <li>ask us to delete your information in certain circumstances;</li>
    <li>ask us to restrict, or object to, our use of your information in certain circumstances;</li>
    <li>ask for your information in a portable format where it applies; and</li>
    <li>withdraw your consent at any time, where we rely on consent.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>To use any of these rights, contact us using the details above. You also have the right to complain to the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO) at <a href="https://ico.org.uk">ico.org.uk</a>. We would appreciate the chance to deal with your concerns first.</p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>We take reasonable steps to protect personal information, including serving our website over an encrypted (HTTPS) connection and limiting who can access it. No online system is completely secure, so please take care about what you send us.</p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>Our <a href="/cookies/">Cookie Policy</a> explains how this website uses cookies.</p>

  <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
  <p>Our website may link to other websites, such as Google. We are not responsible for their privacy practices, so please read their policies.</p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy from time to time. The date at the top shows when it was last changed.</p>
</LegalPage>
